A||||13||mrgone||shifting problem||||4||
Z||000000||mrgone||06-29-2001||05:11 PM||||alot of the time while going into reverse (5speed) it grinds, and i have a hard time shifting into first, sometimes i have to re-engage the clutch. actually once i had a hard time getting into any gear, so i rolled a bit and pumped the clutch and the gears reappeared. i almost got myself in to trouble when pulling into the parking lot, i expected to get into 1st but pushing harder on the stick didnt help. had to reapply clutch. i think i really need my tranny fluid changed. i got the week off, but i wont be able to do anything cause im flying to NS for it.||||reg||4
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-29-2001||05:37 PM||||sounds like your pushrod on the clutch lever(slave cyllinder on the firewall side of the tranny) may need to be adjusted..its not engaging the clutch fully..<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||06-29-2001||07:21 PM||||I would say that one of your cables are out of adjustment you will need someone to help you to make any adjustments and these are the shift cables on the transmision have some one sit in the car and shift slowly while you are looking at the shift mechinisim  just stare at it a little bit while this other person shifts your gears at your comand and I am sure you will be able to figure out what adjustments are needed.Oh you will need a 15 million meter wrench.||||reg||7
Z||000003||sjp777||06-29-2001||08:45 PM||||Check the clutch hydraulics. You can't adjust it other than bleeding to make sure there is no air. If there is air, the master or the slave is probably on it's way out.<P>A clutch that doesn't fully disengage will cause exactly the problem you are describing.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||06-29-2001||09:49 PM||||just went through that. ended up changing mc slave cyl. and thourough bleeding. try a good bleed first before you start buying parts.||||reg||1
Z||000005||c m west||06-29-2001||09:57 PM||||It is your Shift Cable ( NOT Select Cable ) - period<P><BR>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000006||sjp777||06-29-2001||11:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>It is your Shift Cable ( NOT Select Cable ) - period<P><BR>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Everytime someone posts that problem you say that. It is not always going to be a shift cable. In fact, the clutch not fully disengaging is the more common and far more likely cause.<P>Period<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Leadfoot||07-03-2001||11:36 AM||||I had a shifting problem myself.  Turns out the clutch pedal was made of aluminum and bent out of shape.  I replaced the pedal with a steel one and the problem went away.  You might want to check Archie's website.  He describes how to trouble shoot clutch problems. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||sgtoxx||07-03-2001||09:45 PM||||Been there to.  After bleeding and bleeding the hydraulics, wound up being the clutch slave cylinder not engaging the clutch push rod far enough.  Took three visits to the auto parts store and three slave cylinders to find out that the stroke for my 86 Fiero GT with the munsey tranny was 15/16 inch, not 13/16 inch!  That 1/8 inch makes all the difference in the world!||||reg||1
Z||000009||V8Dreamer||07-03-2001||10:57 PM||||mrgone, if you get a chance, email me and lemme know what you find out....I have the EXACT same prob...it's a b*tch to get into 1st sometimes and R almost always emits a most wonderful sound....wuite embarrassing when you're in a parking lot full of people.  And to Chris West, sorry, buy my shift cable is brand new, direct from the dealer.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
