Z||000012||mrgone||07-04-2001||02:33 AM||||yeah i have a brand new shift cable sitting on my bedroom floor. on my old cable, right where its attached to the back before it goes under the console where the ecu is broke and is epoxyed 'temporarily.' THe reason why i havent gotten the cable changed is cause the shop said it would take 3 hours, at 1$ a minute. the 180$ cable was enough, so there it sits. the epoxy is holding pretty good tho. I hope changing the tranny fluid helps, as the P.O. prolly didnt know what oil to put in anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000013||johnt671||07-04-2001||08:13 AM||||I had the same problem with 1st and reverse.  I changed to mobil  in the trans, Valvoline synt. brake fluid in the clutch system, adjusted the cables and followed Archies bleeding directions and I have a great shifting car.||||reg||1
